{
  "v": 1,
  "_note": "Shared recurrence vectors (spec 04_VOICE_SCHEDULE_SPEC rev 2 §B2.4 + Appendix V). V1-V10 are the spec's seeds verbatim; V11+ were worked by hand from the IANA rules (America/Chicago: CDT -5 until 2026-11-01 02:00, CST -6 until 2027-03-14 02:00, CDT -5 until 2027-11-07, and 2028-03-12 DST start; Europe/London BST ends 2026-10-25; Asia/Tokyo +9; Asia/Kolkata +5:30). Expected values are literals: neither the relay nor the app evaluator may recompute them. Semantics: next_instants(schedule, after, n) returns the first n planned UTC instants >= after; a vector whose expect list is shorter than n means 'then none'. Choices the RFC leaves open, fixed here for both evaluators: a dtstart that doesn't match the rule (unsynchronized) is NOT an instance (V20, V33); the week starts on Monday and WKST is ignored (V23, V24); BYMONTHDAY takes one value; numbers are canonical digits (no leading zeros or signs except -1); rule parts may come in any order. The dtstart instance itself is always valid (a dtstart in a DST gap takes the pre-gap offset, V7, V43); a later instance whose local time is in a gap, or whose date doesn't exist, is omitted and not counted (V3, V27, V30).",
